IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation "version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026":
-- PART 10A, TRANSFER OF REGISTRATION: ss 355 and 356 (lines 23148 to 23186 of CoA1967.txt).
-- The Part provides for a transfer of registration INTO Singapore only: a foreign corporate entity becomes a company limited by shares.
--
-- Reading a result here (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sge)"):
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes;
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words (a "means" definition, an "unless", a flat negative);
--   NOTHING     the text does not say (a scope limit, a list not closed, a limit of its own wording, a term it leaves undefined).
-- A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE. Every branch that answers JUST FALSE or NOTHING says which kind, and why, in a comment.
--
-- The facts below are plain facts a witness can state. Where the text hands a matter to another provision, to the regulations or to the
-- Registrar's judgment, the module asks it as an input named for that fact.

§ `Section 355: foreign corporate entities to which this Part applies`

-- s 355 is a scope provision: "This Part applies to a foreign corporate entity which intends to be registered as a company limited by shares".
-- The class is the entity in s 356's sense; whether a body is one is s 356's question, asked there ("foreign corporate entity").
-- src:23154 | 355. This Part applies to a foreign corporate entity which intends to
-- src:23155 | be registered as a company limited by shares under this Act.
@ref s 355 (src:23154-23155)
GIVEN `the body is a foreign corporate entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign corporate entity intends to be registered as a company limited by shares under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 355 this Part applies to the body` MEANS
    IF `the body is a foreign corporate entity` AND `the foreign corporate entity intends to be registered as a company limited by shares under this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This Part applies to a foreign corporate entity which intends to be registered as a company limited by shares under this Act" is a scope limit with no "only" (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (c): outside the scope the answer is NOTHING; fork line F-355 in NOTES.md)

§ `Section 356: the words this Part defines`

-- The opening words: "In this Part, unless the context otherwise requires". Whether the context requires otherwise is a plain input.
-- src:23161 | 356. In this Part, unless the context otherwise requires —
@ref s 356 (src:23161-23161)
GIVEN `the word is one that section 356 defines` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context requires the word to mean something else` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 356 the definition in this section governs the word where it is used` MEANS
    IF NOT `the word is one that section 356 defines`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the opening words speak only of the words the section defines
    ELSE (IF `the context requires the word to mean something else`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Part, unless the context otherwise requires"
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- "date of registration": in relation to an entity that has applied, the date of registration specified in the notice of transfer of registration.
-- src:23163 | “date of registration”, in relation to a foreign corporate entity
-- src:23164 | that has applied to be registered as a company limited by
-- src:23165 | shares under this Part, means the date of registration of the
-- src:23166 | foreign corporate entity specified in the notice of transfer of
-- src:23167 | registration;
@ref s 356 "date of registration" (src:23163-23167)
GIVEN `the foreign corporate entity has applied to be registered as a company limited by shares under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice of transfer of registration has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of registration specified in the notice of transfer of registration` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 356 "date of registration" the date of registration of the foreign corporate entity` MEANS
    IF `the foreign corporate entity has applied to be registered as a company limited by shares under this Part` AND `the notice of transfer of registration has been issued`
    THEN JUST `the date of registration specified in the notice of transfer of registration`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "“date of registration”, in relation to a foreign corporate entity that has applied to be registered ... under this Part, means the date of registration of the foreign corporate entity specified in the notice of transfer of registration": no date exists for an entity that has not applied, or before the notice is issued

-- "foreign corporate entity": a body corporate that is incorporated outside Singapore. A "means" definition: a body that is not both is not one.
-- src:23169 | “foreign corporate entity” means a body corporate that is
-- src:23170 | incorporated outside Singapore;
@ref s 356 "foreign corporate entity" (src:23169-23170)
GIVEN `the body is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is incorporated outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 356 "foreign corporate entity" the body is a foreign corporate entity` MEANS
    IF `the body is a body corporate` AND `the body is incorporated outside Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“foreign corporate entity” means a body corporate that is incorporated outside Singapore"

-- "notice of transfer of registration": the notice issued under section 359(3).
-- src:23172 | “notice of transfer of registration” means the notice of transfer of
-- src:23173 | registration issued under section 359(3);
@ref s 356 "notice of transfer of registration" (src:23172-23173)
GIVEN `the notice is the notice of transfer of registration issued under section 359(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 356 "notice of transfer of registration" the notice is the notice of transfer of registration` MEANS
    IF `the notice is the notice of transfer of registration issued under section 359(3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“notice of transfer of registration” means the notice of transfer of registration issued under section 359(3)"

-- "place of incorporation": for an entity that transferred its domicile after incorporation, the jurisdiction where it is domiciled when it applies.
-- For any other entity the definition says nothing, and so does this function.
-- src:23175 | “place of incorporation” means, in the case of a foreign
-- src:23176 | corporate entity that had transferred its domicile after its
-- src:23177 | incorporation, the jurisdiction where the foreign corporate
-- src:23178 | entity is domiciled at the time it applies for registration;
@ref s 356 "place of incorporation" (src:23175-23178)
GIVEN `the foreign corporate entity had transferred its domicile after its incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the jurisdiction where the foreign corporate entity is domiciled at the time it applies for registration` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 356 "place of incorporation" the place of incorporation of the foreign corporate entity` MEANS
    IF `the foreign corporate entity had transferred its domicile after its incorporation`
    THEN JUST `the jurisdiction where the foreign corporate entity is domiciled at the time it applies for registration`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "“place of incorporation” means, in the case of a foreign corporate entity that had transferred its domicile after its incorporation, the jurisdiction where the foreign corporate entity is domiciled at the time it applies for registration": the definition is given only for that case

-- "registration": registration by the Registrar under section 359(1), in relation to an entity that has applied.
-- src:23180 | “registration”, in relation to a foreign corporate entity that has
-- src:23181 | applied to be registered as a company limited by shares under
-- src:23182 | this Part, means registration by the Registrar under
-- src:23183 | section 359(1), and “register” and “registered” are to be
-- src:23184 | construed accordingly.
@ref s 356 "registration" (src:23180-23184)
GIVEN `the foreign corporate entity has applied to be registered as a company limited by shares under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is registration by the Registrar under section 359(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 356 "registration" the act is registration of the foreign corporate entity` MEANS
    IF NOT `the foreign corporate entity has applied to be registered as a company limited by shares under this Part`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "“registration”, in relation to a foreign corporate entity that has applied to be registered ... under this Part, means registration by the Registrar under section 359(1)": defined for an entity that has applied
    ELSE (IF `the act is registration by the Registrar under section 359(1)`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means registration by the Registrar under section 359(1)"

-- "register" and "registered" are "construed accordingly": an entity is registered when the Registrar has registered it under section 359(1).
-- src:23183 | section 359(1), and “register” and “registered” are to be
-- src:23184 | construed accordingly.
@ref s 356 "registration" (src:23183-23184)
GIVEN `the foreign corporate entity has applied to be registered as a company limited by shares under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has registered the foreign corporate entity under section 359(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 356 "register" and "registered" the foreign corporate entity is registered` MEANS
    IF NOT `the foreign corporate entity has applied to be registered as a company limited by shares under this Part`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "“register” and “registered” are to be construed accordingly", that is, in relation to an entity that has applied
    ELSE (IF `the Registrar has registered the foreign corporate entity under section 359(1)`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“register” and “registered” are to be construed accordingly" (as registration by the Registrar under section 359(1))
